        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>7821 Akuji is a short, liminal horror experience where you pilot a makeshift submarine inside a liquid filled asteroid, searching for a lost science crew.</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Story:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; loading decryption key 77CX223UI2F9</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… packet checksum validated </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… decryption successful </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… decompressing data blob.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… complete</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; data stream follows:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency Log Entry 00</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Something is up, power went off hours ago. Backups didn't kick in. Everything is dark and my o2 allocation is running out. What is going on? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Door controls are dead and I hear nothing outside. I hope someone gets this door open soon. My head is starting to ache…  . Hope this isn't my last log.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency Log Entry 01</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I’m pretty sure I blacked out from the lack of oxygen. Barely awake when some Enforcers dragged me to the bridge and gave me two choices: accept a brain wipe for the last few weeks and return to Galene, or pilot some… submersible they made to find a lost science crew?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I know what those brain wipes did to other people, I ain’t gonna risk it. Plus Riley was assigned to the science crew - and if I succeeded in this task I was promised a 3rd class citizenship. Easy choice. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Back in my room now. They left an o2 canister. At least I can breathe.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency log entry 02</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I can hear them coming for me. If I can't find you Riley. Know that… I might be in love with you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <i> Press any key to continue.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Gameplay:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Navigate your submersible that is barely water tight through tight corridors with only a single light to guide your way.The hacked-together submersible only has a tiny porthole for you to navigate.Choose two routes: Be a good corporate employee and get the job done. Or choose an alternative path...Pick up items, keycards and solve puzzles in order to progress and reach the lost submarine!</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Game Developer Notes:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I developed this game at 1440p, with an amd 7900 cpu and a 4060 gpu. These specs allow me to get 90+ fps native. I've included an upscale feature and it will let me hit over 200fps. I hope that the art style and graphics options will allow older pcs to play at a good framerate.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I've also included options for ray traced shadows (some performance hit if enabled) and other engine-related optimization features but you really don't need to mess around with them.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>7821 Akuji is a short, liminal horror experience where you pilot a makeshift submarine inside a liquid filled asteroid, searching for a lost science crew.</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Story:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; loading decryption key 77CX223UI2F9</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… packet checksum validated </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… decryption successful </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… decompressing data blob.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; ………… complete</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >&gt; data stream follows:</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency Log Entry 00</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Something is up, power went off hours ago. Backups didn't kick in. Everything is dark and my o2 allocation is running out. What is going on? </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Door controls are dead and I hear nothing outside. I hope someone gets this door open soon. My head is starting to ache…  . Hope this isn't my last log.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency Log Entry 01</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I’m pretty sure I blacked out from the lack of oxygen. Barely awake when some Enforcers dragged me to the bridge and gave me two choices: accept a brain wipe for the last few weeks and return to Galene, or pilot some… submersible they made to find a lost science crew?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I know what those brain wipes did to other people, I ain’t gonna risk it. Plus Riley was assigned to the science crew - and if I succeeded in this task I was promised a 3rd class citizenship. Easy choice. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Back in my room now. They left an o2 canister. At least I can breathe.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Emergency log entry 02</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I can hear them coming for me. If I can't find you Riley. Know that… I might be in love with you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <i> Press any key to continue.</i></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Gameplay:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Navigate your submersible that is barely water tight through tight corridors with only a single light to guide your way.The hacked-together submersible only has a tiny porthole for you to navigate.Choose two routes: Be a good corporate employee and get the job done. Or choose an alternative path...Pick up items, keycards and solve puzzles in order to progress and reach the lost submarine!</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Game Developer Notes:</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I developed this game at 1440p, with an amd 7900 cpu and a 4060 gpu. These specs allow me to get 90+ fps native. I've included an upscale feature and it will let me hit over 200fps. I hope that the art style and graphics options will allow older pcs to play at a good framerate.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >I've also included options for ray traced shadows (some performance hit if enabled) and other engine-related optimization features but you really don't need to mess around with them.</p>",
